<</Names[(NDIS226_Dashboard_Psychosocial_Sep23_P4.indd:1. The Australian Bureau of Statistics SEIFA Index of Education and Occupation \(IEO\) is used by NDIA:21)[6 0 R/XYZ 22 520 null](NDIS226_Dashboard_Psychosocial_Sep23_P4.indd:10.  A registered provider is an approved person or provider of supports who is registered with the:30)[6 0 R/XYZ 22 182 null](NDIS226_Dashboard_Psychosocial_Sep23_P4.indd:2. Supported Independent Living \(SIL\) is help with and/or supervision of daily tasks to develop the:22)[6 0 R/XYZ 22 459 null](NDIS226_Dashboard_Psychosocial_Sep23_P4.indd:3. Average payments per participant are calculated using a 12 month period prior to the reporting da:23)[6 0 R/XYZ 22 435 null](NDIS226_Dashboard_Psychosocial_Sep23_P4.indd:4. The average payment for the same group of participants is compared across two different time peri:24)[6 0 R/XYZ 22 421 null](NDIS226_Dashboard_Psychosocial_Sep23_P4.indd:5. The Participant Outcome section compares baseline results when participants entered the Scheme or:25)[6 0 R/XYZ 22 381 null](NDIS226_Dashboard_Psychosocial_Sep23_P4.indd:6. The NDIA gathers responses at the four primary stages of the participant pathway - access, pre-pl:26)[6 0 R/XYZ 22 320 null](NDIS226_Dashboard_Psychosocial_Sep23_P4.indd:7. The complaint rate is an annualised rate calculated as the number of complaints in the quarter di:27)[6 0 R/XYZ 22 281 null](NDIS226_Dashboard_Psychosocial_Sep23_P4.indd:8. The count of providers is by ABN and includes providers supporting agency-managed participants, p:28)[6 0 R/XYZ 22 252 null](NDIS226_Dashboard_Psychosocial_Sep23_P4.indd:9. For each plan management type, a single provider is counted if they received a payment in the qua:29)[6 0 R/XYZ 22 217 null](NDIS226_Dashboard_Psychosocial_Sep23_P4.indd:Insights:15)[12 0 R/XYZ 22 1292 null](NDIS226_Dashboard_Psychosocial_Sep23_P4.indd:Insights:33)[12 0 R/XYZ 22 1292 null](NDIS226_Dashboard_Psychosocial_Sep23_P4.indd:Insights:9)[12 0 R/XYZ 22 1292 null](NDIS226_Dashboard_Psychosocial_Sep23_P4.indd:Key definitions:20)[6 0 R/XYZ 22 587 null](NDIS226_Dashboard_Psychosocial_Sep23_P4.indd:Key definitions:32)[6 0 R/XYZ 22 587 null](NDIS226_Dashboard_Psychosocial_Sep23_P4.indd:Section 1: Participants:10)[89 0 R/XYZ 23 1064 null](NDIS226_Dashboard_Psychosocial_Sep23_P4.indd:Section 1: Participants:16)[89 0 R/XYZ 23 1064 null](NDIS226_Dashboard_Psychosocial_Sep23_P4.indd:Section 2: Payments:11)[164 0 R/XYZ 22 1337 null](NDIS226_Dashboard_Psychosocial_Sep23_P4.indd:Section 2: Payments:17)[164 0 R/XYZ 22 1337 null](NDIS226_Dashboard_Psychosocial_Sep23_P4.indd:Section 3: Participant outcomes and satisfaction:18)[180 0 R/XYZ 22 958 null](NDIS226_Dashboard_Psychosocial_Sep23_P4.indd:Section 4: Providers:13)[255 0 R/XYZ 22 878 null](NDIS226_Dashboard_Psychosocial_Sep23_P4.indd:Section 4: Providers:19)[255 0 R/XYZ 22 878 null]]>>
